      "content": "When I mentioned \"complex\" culture in Nigeria, I was referring to the dense network of relationships and hierarchies that can influence business interactions. This can sometimes lead to imprecision in communication, misunderstandings, or fluctuations in delivery timelines. Corruption and bureaucratic corruption are notable concerns, particularly with land acquisition, customs declarations, and payments.\n\nHowever, reputable Nigerian suppliers tend to prioritize professionalism, and you can typically find reliable partners among trusted contacts or through established suppliers. The key is building strong relationships with key stakeholders, such as key account managers, business development managers, or department heads.",
